// std/time_affine.dag -- Affine time COORDINATES over the elapsed-time group.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS (facts-first; named consumer = ctrl#1612 / gunbc#4883
// ProbeSelector host-health burn-in `TemporalAggregator`):
//   A health / burn-in aggregator distinguishes time INSTANTS (`now`,
//   `first_failed_at`) from a DURATION threshold (`min_down`). Instants are
//   affine COORDINATES on a time axis: you cannot ADD two instants, you
//   SUBTRACT them to obtain a duration. The drain predicate is
//   `(now - first_failed_at) >= min_down` -- instant - instant -> duration,
//   then a duration-vs-duration comparison. Modeling all three as a flat
//   `Int` (the #4883 form-3 unit violation: `now_ms`/`first_failed_at_ms`/
//   `min_down_ms: Int`) conflates a coordinate with a magnitude and discards
//   the affine discipline -- it lets `now + first_failed_at` type-check, which
//   is meaningless.
//
// STRUCTURE (bold-crane modeling ruling, 2026-06-15): `Instant` is a torsor
//   (an affine space) over the abelian group of elapsed time. The elapsed-time
//   group is std.measure `Measure<Time, Milli>` -- additive: durations add,
//   identity = zero elapsed, inverse = the time-reversed offset. `Instant` is
//   the torsor's point set; the action is `instant + duration -> instant`; the
//   difference is `instant - instant -> duration`. `instant + instant` is NOT
//   an operation.
//
// GENERALIZATION (DEFERRED to the carrier authority = snappy): this is the
//   SAME affine/torsor shape as SPICE's `AbsolutePotential` (point) over
//   `PotentialDifference` (group) -- gentle-lynx #4895 / #4913. When SPICE
//   becomes the SECOND inhabitant, snappy lifts ONE general
//   `Torsor<Point, Group>` (point-over-additive-group) carrier and re-expresses
//   BOTH time and potential on it. Per facts-first / construction-over-ratchets
//   this file ships ONLY the concrete inhabited TIME instantiation now -- it
//   does NOT stand up a standalone uninhabited abstract group surface (the
//   uninhabited-generality anti-pattern). gentle-lynx's SPICE torsor MUST
//   CONVERGE onto the lifted carrier rather than mint a second time-affine
//   type.
//
// NOT in scope here (tracked dissolution, not defer-and-forget):
//   - Executable affine arithmetic -- the `difference` / `translate` bodies
//     and the `>=` comparison -- is value-level over the phantom `Measure`
//     carrier. It lands when value-typed `Measure` inhabitants arrive (snappy
//     #4885 / the v2 value-read flip), the SAME deferral measure.dag applies
//     to its own value-level ops. THIS file is the TYPE-level affine structure;
//     the lowering is the dissolution, not a missing body to hand-roll.
//
// SUBSTRATE FINDING (still-wren, 2026-06-15, pinned gunbc 81829fc2):
//   `Milliseconds` is modeled as an OPAQUE carrier below, NOT yet aliased to
//   `Measure<Time, Milli>`, for a hard substrate reason: in the pinned tree
//   `Measure<Q, S>` is NOT consumable. (1) dsl/std/measure.dag is 🟡 SCAFFOLD
//   and its enum-VARIANT type-params do not resolve -- `gunbc compile` reports
//   `unresolved type 'One' / 'Time' / 'Memory'` on measure.dag's OWN `ByteSize`
//   / `Hertz`, so every consumer that pulls measure.dag into the closure fails
//   (rust AND dag targets). (2) v4 (src/v4/std) has NO measure.dag at all --
//   which is exactly why #4883's `TemporalAggregator` used bare `Int`. So a
//   literal `type Milliseconds = Measure<Time, Milli>` does NOT compile against
//   the pin today. The affine instant/duration STRUCTURE is the modeling
//   content bold-crane ruled on, and it stands independently of the duration's
//   group spelling. DISSOLVE-ON: when `Measure<Q, S>` becomes consumable
//   (snappy value-Measure / #4885 / the flip-SHA), re-point `Milliseconds` to
//   `Measure<Time, Milli>` (one-line change; all call sites keep type-checking).

module std.time_affine

// --- Milliseconds: the additive time-magnitude group element ------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 P-TIME-ELAPSED-CARRIER -- opaque elapsed-time
//   DURATION at millisecond scale; the abelian group over which `Instant` is
//   affine. Opaque pending Measure-consumability (see SUBSTRATE FINDING in the
//   header). Dissolve-on: re-point to `Measure<Time, Milli>` when snappy's
//   value-Measure lands.
//
// M9 NOTE: std.compute_fabric already aliases `Duration = Measure<Time, One>`
// (seconds) -- scale is a `Measure` PARAMETER, not a distinct concept, so on
// the dissolution this becomes `Measure<Time, Milli>` rather than a re-minted
// `Duration`. measure.dag's forward-flagged scale-agnostic `Duration<S>`
// (>= 2 consumers) would subsume both; until then this is the named
// millisecond consumer the #4883 fields demand.
//
// Opaque nominal carrier (empty record = no runtime payload, the phantom
// discipline) so it cargo-checks today; a bodyless `type Milliseconds` would
// emit a recursive Rust alias. Re-points to `Measure<Time, Milli>` on the
// dissolution.
type Milliseconds {}

// --- Instant: an affine time coordinate ------------------------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 P-TIME-AFFINE -- phantom affine-coordinate carrier.
//   Dissolve-on: (a) snappy lifts the general point-over-additive-group torsor
//   carrier once SPICE is the 2nd inhabitant, at which point `Instant` becomes
//   `Torsor<Instant, Milliseconds>` (or the ratified spelling); AND (b) value-
//   typed `Measure` inhabitants land so the affine arithmetic becomes
//   executable.
//
// Phantom carrier -- no runtime payload at this layer, the same discipline as
// `Measure<Q, S>`. Semantics: a coordinate on the millisecond time axis.
// Affine over `Milliseconds`:
//   - difference(later, earlier) : Instant - Instant -> Milliseconds  (torsor subtraction)
//   - translate(base, delta)     : Instant + Milliseconds -> Instant  (group action)
//   - there is NO `Instant + Instant` -- adding two coordinates is undefined.
//
// Opaque nominal carrier (empty record = no runtime payload, the phantom
// discipline) so it cargo-checks today; a bodyless `type Instant` emits a
// recursive Rust alias. The point-set gains structure (and the affine ops
// gain bodies) on the dissolution.
type Instant {}

// --- TimeAffine: the concrete (time-specific) torsor operations ------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 P-TIME-AFFINE-OPS -- concrete op dictionary for
//   `Instant` over `Milliseconds`. CONCRETE, not a generic `Torsor<P, G>`: per the
//   facts-first steer we ship the inhabited time instantiation and leave the
//   generic lift to snappy at ratification. The fn-typed fields express the
//   affine algebra at the TYPE level; executable bodies are the deferred
//   value-Measure lowering (see header). Dissolve-on: the generic torsor lift.
type TimeAffine {
  difference: fn(Instant, Instant) -> Milliseconds
  translate:  fn(Instant, Milliseconds) -> Instant
}

// --- DrainWindow: the inhabited named-consumer witness ---------------------
//
// PRACTICE 4 CHECKPOINT: 🟡 P-TIME-AFFINE-CONSUMER -- the #4883 host-health
//   burn-in drain window re-typed off the affine carrier. The form-3 `Int`
//   fields become `Instant` (coordinate) + `Milliseconds` (duration), which
//   eliminates the unit violation. This is the inhabitance that JUSTIFIES the
//   carrier (facts-first) and the compile-witness that `Instant` / `Milliseconds`
//   slot into a struct. Single authority for the full aggregator remains
//   probe_selector's `TemporalAggregator`; it adopts this shape at the dsl/std
//   relocation. Dissolve-on: the relocated `TemporalAggregator` consumes
//   `Instant` / `Milliseconds` directly, retiring this witness.
type DrainWindow {
  first_failed_at: Instant      // was first_failed_at_ms: Int  (affine coordinate)
  min_down: Milliseconds           // was min_down_ms: Int          (additive duration)
}
